FUNCTIONS:

func greeting() {
    print("Welcome to Swift Programming")----->Welcome to Swift Programming
}
greeting()

\\-->A function is a reusable block of code that performs a particular task.
--->Instead of writing the same code repeatedly, you can create a function and call it whenever needed.

Functions with Parameters:

func add(a: Int, b: Int) {
    print(a + b)
}
add(a: 10, b: 20)

\\Parameters allow us to pass values into a function.

FUNCTION WITH RETURN VALUE:

//Functions can also return a result
func multiply(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {
    return a * b
}
let result = multiply(a: 5, b: 4)
print(result)---->20
